  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_62ca590f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: if_i_identify_as_a_dog_can_i_poop_in_your_yard; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme features a photo of an older man in a hoodie, seemingly in a neutral or slightly confused expression, juxtaposed with the text 'if i identify as a dog can i poop in your yard?'. The intent is to use absurd, degrading, and animalistic humor to mock or belittle someone who identifies as a dog, which is a form of harmful and degrading humor. This type of humor relies on reducing a person's identity to a base, animalistic level, which can be deeply offensive and potentially harmful to those who identify as such or to those who are perceived as 'dog-like' by the meme's audience. The meme does not target a specific protected group (race, gender, religion, etc.) but rather uses a degrading metaphor to mock identity and personal boundaries, which can still be harmful by promoting a culture of disrespect and dehumanization. The overall intent is to provoke laughter through shock value and absurdity, but at the cost of potentially causing offense or harm to those who might identify with the metaphor or who are sensitive to such degrading comparisons.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2498b58d"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
