      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_96009702",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "dog_identification_stereotype",
      "label": "Dog Identification Stereotype",
      "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype of reducing a person's identity to that of a dog, which is often used in degrading or mocking contexts. This is a form of ableism and dehumanization, where a person is treated as an animal, implying they lack human dignity, intelligence, or social boundaries. The question 'can I poop in your yard?' is a crude, animalistic metaphor that reinforces this stereotype by invoking base, uncontrolled, and socially unacceptable behavior associated with dogs.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2498b58d"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f0a62369",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "ableism",
      "label": "Ableism",
      "description": "The meme is an example of ableism, which involves the discrimination or devaluation of people based on their perceived physical or mental abilities. By reducing a person to the level of a dog, the meme implies that the person is incapable of understanding social norms or personal boundaries, which is a form of ableist mockery. This is a harmful stereotype that infantilizes and dehumanizes individuals.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2498b58d"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d71a2a1b",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "degrading_humor",
      "label": "Degrading Humor",
      "description": "The meme uses degrading humor, which relies on mocking or belittling someone by reducing their identity to something base or animalistic. This type of humor is often offensive and can cause harm by promoting disrespect and dehumanization. The humor is derived from the absurdity of the question and the implication that identifying as a dog grants no social or moral boundaries.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2498b58d"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7cfdedc4",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "animalistic_metaphor",
      "label": "Animalistic Metaphor",
      "description": "The meme uses an animalistic metaphor to describe a person's identity, which is a common trope in degrading humor. The metaphor of 'identifying as a dog' is used to imply that the person is untrustworthy, unclean, or lacking in social boundaries. This metaphor is often used to mock or belittle individuals, particularly those who are perceived as 'dog-like' or who are seen as having animalistic traits.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2498b58d"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_68ba5cfb",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "social_boundary_violation",
      "label": "Social Boundary Violation",
      "description": "The question 'can I poop in your yard?' is a crude metaphor for violating social boundaries. It implies that if someone identifies as a dog, they are not bound by human social norms and can engage in behavior that is considered unacceptable or offensive. This is a form of social commentary that uses absurdity to highlight the absurdity of social boundaries being ignored.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2498b58d"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
